cff-version: 1.2.0
title: pdfnative-mcp
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: Nizoka
    website: "https://github.com/Nizoka"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nizoka/pdfnative-mcp"
url: "https://github.com/Nizoka/pdfnative-mcp"
abstract: >-
  Model Context Protocol (MCP) server bridging the zero-dependency pdfnative
  library to AI clients. Provides 28 production-grade tools for PDF generation
  (13 document block kinds, page layout options, fine typography, right-to-left
  text, operator-supplied fonts, a read-only pagination preview), PDF/A archival
  with embedded fonts and conformance diagnostics, PDF/X-4 print exchange (alone
  or as a dual claim with PDF/A-2), PDF/UA structural validation, native vector
  charts, embedded barcodes, text in 32 Unicode scripts, JPEG / PNG / JPEG 2000
  images, CMYK and spot colours, smart tables, interactive forms (create, read,
  fill, flatten), embedded files (Factur-X), digital signatures with the full
  PAdES long-term-validation ladder (B-B to B-LTA: RFC 3161 timestamps, DSS,
  document timestamps) and verification, print production (page boxes, bleed,
  printer's marks, colour bars), reproducible output, document metadata
  updates, encryption round-trip, page-tree operations, markup and link
  annotations, Unicode text extraction, PDF introspection, and human-in-the-loop
  governance issue drafting. Speaks MCP 2026-07-28 with automatic fallback for
  2025-era clients, makes no outbound network call by default, is fuzzed
  continuously and published with provenance and SBOMs.
license: MIT
version: 1.8.0
date-released: "2026-10-31"
